{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c interface implementation c interface implementation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","fileName":"C# Interface Implementation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Interface Implementation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c interface implementation c interface implementation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","fileName":"C# Interface Implementation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Interface Implementation","heading":"C# Interface Implementation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A C# interface declares capabilities a type promises to provide. Code can depend on that contract rather than a specific class, allowing different implementations to participate wherever the same operations are required.\n\nCommon .NET interfaces support comparison, enumeration, formatting, serialization, and deterministic disposal. Implementation can be public or explicit; explicit members are reached through the interface view and help separate overlapping contracts from the class's ordinary surface.\n\nAn interface can declare methods, properties, events, and indexers that an implementing class must provide. Because a class can implement several interfaces, each interface can express one focused capability without forcing an unrelated implementation hierarchy.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c interface implementation c interface implementation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Interface Implementation.md","fileName":"C# Interface Implementation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Interface Implementation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}